From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omacut-windows prepare-source <prepare-source@omacut-windows.invalid>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:13:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add every video of a drop on Qt 6.8

Dropping files on the window hands their urls to Backend::addVideos() as
a QVariantList. On the Qt 6.8 this port builds with, each entry is a
QVariant holding a QVariant that holds the QUrl, and toUrl() on that
outer QVariant gives an empty url. Every file of every drop was then
refused as not a local path, so a drop never opened or added anything.

Unwrap the one extra level with qvariant_cast<QVariant>, which leaves a
QVariant that already holds the QUrl as it is. The QML drop tests cover
it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/backend.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backend.cpp b/src/backend.cpp
index d831ee4c0cb76a87d72637db5de86353ddff16d6..35cda4644f19f10b0b3705c55a092c8d80db4dd2 100644
--- a/src/backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backend.cpp
@@ -349,7 +349,11 @@ bool Backend::addVideos(const QVariantList &urls, double t) {
     int queued = 0;
     for (const QVariant &value : urls) {
         PendingVideo pending;
-        pending.url = value.toUrl();
+        // A drop's url list can reach here as QVariants that each hold a
+        // QVariant holding the QUrl (Qt 6.8 does), which toUrl() reads as
+        // empty; qvariant_cast<QVariant> unwraps one level, and is a no-op
+        // on a variant that already holds the QUrl.
+        pending.url = qvariant_cast<QVariant>(value).toUrl();
         pending.adding = true;
         pending.chain = true;
         pending.addAt = t;
